  "goodToKnow": "Die Ungnade is disfavour or disgrace, used almost only in bei jemandem in Ungnade fallen (to fall out of favour) and sich jemandes Ungnade zuziehen. It comes from court language, when subjects depended on a ruler's Gnade (favour, mercy). Die Gnade also means grace and mercy: um Gnade bitten, das Gnadengesuch (petition for clemency). Gnadenlos means merciless. It has no plural."
